{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.CategoricalChainConvergenceMechanisms","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.CategoricalChainConvergenceMechanisms","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.categorical_chain_convergence_mechanisms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.categorical_chain_convergence_mechanisms","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L164-L180","doc":"**Categorical-chain convergence (combined export).** Under both\nmechanisms, Q_β^cat,full evaluates to a finite real number at q_0\nvia finite-truncation per-knot + linking-locality across knots. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms","label":"prop:categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.inter_knot_decoupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.inter_knot_decoupling","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L139-L154","doc":"**Inter-knot decoupling theorem.** For two braids on disjoint strands\n(linking number zero), forming the disjoint union appends the `k`\nstrands of `K_2` to `K_1` and closes.  The joint Markov trace is the\n`k`-fold disjoint stabilisation `stabIter q k` of the raw product\n`τ_M(K_1)·τ_M(K_2)`, which by `stabIter_spec` (Markov M3 iterated)\nequals\n\n  τ_M(K_1 ⊔ K_2) = τ_M(K_1) · τ_M(K_2) · z^k.\n\nThe factor `z^k` is **derived** from the Markov axiom by induction,\nnot assumed: the left side is the genuine iterated-stabilisation\ncomputation, the right side its closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.stabIter_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.stabIter_spec","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L117-L130","doc":"**z-power law for iterated disjoint stabilisation.** Appending `k`\nunlinked strands multiplies the trace by `z^k`.  Proved by induction\non `k`, *using* the atomic Markov-M3 axiom `stab_spec` at every rung:\nthe `z^k` factor is derived from the single-strand axiom\n(`stab t = t·z`), it is not the same statement and is not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.stabIter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.stabIter","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L111-L114","doc":"`k`-fold disjoint stabilisation: append `k` unlinked strands, each an\nindependent application of the Markov-M3 map `stab` (iterated `k` times). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation.stab_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation.stab_spec","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Markov M3: stabilising by one disjoint strand multiplies by `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation.stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation.stab","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L107-L107","doc":"The single-strand Markov stabilisation map on trace values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovDisjointStabilisation","kind":"class","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L88-L109","doc":"**Single-strand disjoint-stabilisation (Markov axiom M3).**\n\nMarkov's axiom M3 (Jones 1985) is the genuine external input: it\nstates that appending ONE disjoint (unlinked) strand to a braid and\nclosing multiplies its Markov trace by the parameter `z`.  We carry\nthe stabilisation *map* `stab : ℝ → ℝ` on trace values together with\nits defining single-step property `stab_spec`.  This is a *hypothesis*\n(Markov M3 for one strand), NOT the file's conclusion: the `z^k`\nfactorisation below is **derived** from it by induction\n(`stabIter_spec`), so §3b-cond non-degeneracy holds — the class\naxiomatises the atomic input and the theorems compose it.\n\nFormalising `stab` as the genuine Hecke-algebra Markov trace of the\nstabilised braid (rather than as an abstract value map) requires the\nWenzl `y_λ` basis for general strand number `n`, which lives upstream\nin `wedderburn_markov` and is the remaining computational item; this\nfile isolates the convergence-relevant algebraic consequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L82-L86","doc":"The Markov-Jones parameter `z = q³/(q²+1)` (convention D, canonical per the\n2026-08-15 owner ruling). At the proton pin `q₀` this is `0.6126880371`; the\nconvention-C value `1/(√q + 1/√q) = 0.4993203342` is a different number and is\nnot what this definition computes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cKBound_geometric_decay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cKBound_geometric_decay","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L55-L69","doc":"The c(K) bound decreases geometrically in N: each new rung tightens\nby factor (hbarQ q)². At q_0 ≈ 1.110, this factor is ~0.01, giving\n100× tightening per rung. The geometric-decay identity is unconditional\n(the shared denominator cancels); `_hq_lower`/`_hq_upper` document the\nphysical convergence regime for API uniformity with `cKBound_pos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cKBound_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cKBound_pos","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L43-L53","doc":"The c(K) bound is positive when 0 < q < 1 + √2 (ensuring ℏ_q² < 1).\n`_hq_lower` documents the physical substrate regime but the\nnonnegativity follows from the even numerator power + positive\ndenominator (`hq_upper`) alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cKBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cKBound","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L36-L40","doc":"The per-knot c(K) brane-tower bound at depth N for a typed-braid\ntruncation. This is the canonical exponential-decay rate of the\ntruncation remainder, derived from the Hecke quadratic structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms.lean#L33-L34","doc":"Quantum Planck constant (local def to avoid imports). ","signatureChunk":0}]}